1
00:00:25,130 --> 00:00:29,460
[Live Forever]

2
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:32,920
[Episode 5]

3
00:00:34,030 --> 00:00:35,710
But whenever I look at them,

4
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:37,280
I feel

5
00:00:37,730 --> 00:00:39,860
that the soul behind these paintings,

6
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,130
no matter how much time has passed,

7
00:00:43,430 --> 00:00:45,230
or how many names they've taken,

8
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:48,930
seems to have been
the same person all along.

9
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:51,200
Someone

10
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:54,540
I have loved with all my heart.

11
00:01:03,790 --> 00:01:05,250
Autumn Moon in the Forest.

12
00:01:06,490 --> 00:01:07,630
Autumn Moon in the Forest

13
00:01:07,630 --> 00:01:08,380
is over here.

14
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:21,700
This is Autumn Moon in the Forest.

15
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:23,480
It has no artist's signature either,

16
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:25,140
nor any record of provenance.

17
00:01:25,270 --> 00:01:26,480
Yet to me,

18
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,430
there's something
strangely familiar about it.

19
00:01:28,430 --> 00:01:30,630
As if it was always meant to belong here.

20
00:01:31,039 --> 00:01:31,840
What a shame.

21
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:33,580
It's only here on temporary deposit.

22
00:01:33,580 --> 00:01:35,910
It's not part of the museum's collection.

23
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,410
Qiu's feeling a little unwell.

24
00:01:43,410 --> 00:01:44,810
I'll take her home first.

25
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:00,620
This is far enough.

26
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,290
Director Lin, please stay.

27
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:06,120
Miss Song,

28
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:07,560
are you all right?

29
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:12,190
We're sorry for dropping by
unannounced today.

30
00:02:12,190 --> 00:02:14,790
Thank you for
your hospitality, Director Lin.

31
00:02:15,030 --> 00:02:16,290
The pleasure was mine.

32
00:02:16,710 --> 00:02:19,370
Perhaps the two of you and I
are somehow meant to cross paths.

33
00:02:19,370 --> 00:02:20,570
Miss Song seemed

34
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:22,800
particularly moved
by those paintings today.

35
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,910
If you don't mind,

36
00:02:23,910 --> 00:02:25,530
could we exchange contact information?

37
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:26,720
If you'd like to come back later,

38
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:28,180
feel free to stop by anytime.

39
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:28,900
Sorry,

40
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:30,020
she'd rather not.

41
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:31,030
Sure.

42
00:02:58,750 --> 00:02:59,560
Thank you.

43
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:39,560
Ning Changyue, what's gotten into you?

44
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:42,230
Don't tell me you don't recognize him.

45
00:03:42,230 --> 00:03:43,260
He's Lin Huai.

46
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:44,170
Look at the way he looks at you.

47
00:03:44,170 --> 00:03:45,500
So what if he's Lin Huai?

48
00:03:45,950 --> 00:03:47,350
He's been reincarnated.

49
00:03:47,630 --> 00:03:48,430
He's crossed the Bridge of Forgetfulness

50
00:03:48,430 --> 00:03:49,360
and drunk the Potion of Oblivion.

51
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,560
He's forgotten his past lives long ago.

52
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:54,180
He's just an ordinary modern man now,

53
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:55,840
a man who happens to collect paintings.

54
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:56,800
An ordinary man?

55
00:03:56,910 --> 00:03:58,470
Would an ordinary man go out of his way
to collect every painting

56
00:03:58,470 --> 00:04:00,280
you've made over the past 3,000 years?

57
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:01,000
Are you lying to me,

58
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,600
or are you lying to yourself?

59
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:14,070
Where are you going?

60
00:04:14,090 --> 00:04:15,940
I don't like people touching my car.

61
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:16,620
It's dirty.

62
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:18,570
I'm getting it washed.

63
00:04:44,350 --> 00:04:45,280
Ning Changyue,

64
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:49,650
I don't know
what kind of fit you're throwing,

65
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:50,720
but wasn't our common goal

66
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,270
to find the map of the pact

67
00:04:52,270 --> 00:04:54,130
and put an end to our immortality?

68
00:05:04,290 --> 00:05:05,750
You saw it yourself today.

69
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:09,000
Autumn Moon in the Forest
is at the Autumn Art Gallery.

70
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,200
So we'll inevitably

71
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:12,550
have to deal with Director Lin more often.

72
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:26,360
If you don't like it,

73
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,360
I can go by myself.

74
00:05:28,830 --> 00:05:29,890
And another thing,

75
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:31,680
we've been together

76
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,190
for more than 20 years,

77
00:05:33,550 --> 00:05:35,310
but we're not really
husband and wife anymore.

78
00:05:35,310 --> 00:05:36,510
We both know that.

79
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:37,560
So you don't need to

80
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:39,159
put on this jealous act.

81
00:05:41,159 --> 00:05:41,950
An act?

82
00:05:43,750 --> 00:05:46,080
You're right.
I don't need to put on an act.

83
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:05,680
♪ My heart aches as if
it's tearing through my chest ♪

84
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:10,830
♪ Shattered into pieces ♪

85
00:06:11,690 --> 00:06:16,280
♪ Until my lungs have nothing left ♪

86
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:29,210
What is wrong with you?

87
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:41,800
♪ My heart aches as if
it's tearing through my chest ♪

88
00:06:41,850 --> 00:06:46,880
♪ Shattered into pieces ♪

89
00:06:47,610 --> 00:06:51,900
♪ Until my lungs have nothing left ♪

90
00:06:54,490 --> 00:06:59,909
♪ I give up all that was beautiful,
just to find release ♪

91
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:58,430
Song Yiqiu.

92
00:06:59,930 --> 00:07:05,220
♪ Leave it all behind
and run away with me ♪

93
00:07:01,430 --> 00:07:03,160
If I really dropped the act,

94
00:07:04,630 --> 00:07:05,920
could you handle it?

95
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:09,250
♪ Leaving all tenderness behind,
escaping this torment ♪

96
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:44,510
Ning Changyue, what were you doing?

97
00:08:25,950 --> 00:08:26,750
Why?

98
00:08:34,750 --> 00:08:37,210
Why do your eyes look so familiar?

99
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,040
Morning.

100
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:16,150
Morning.

101
00:09:19,790 --> 00:09:21,790
-I was going to...
-I'll first go...

102
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:25,080
-I was just...
-I'm going to the bathroom.

103
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:27,660
-Actually, I...
-Then I'll have breakfast.

104
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:35,920
Are you two all right?

105
00:09:36,150 --> 00:09:37,610
-We're fine.
-We're fine.

106
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:38,860
-I...
-I...

107
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:40,360
We're fine.

108
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:42,000
What could possibly be wrong between us?

109
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:42,530
Exactly.

110
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:45,960
There's something.

111
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,020
I just remembered.

112
00:09:47,150 --> 00:09:48,750
I have somewhere to be today.

113
00:09:48,790 --> 00:09:50,200
I need to go now.

114
00:09:50,510 --> 00:09:52,040
I... I'm just going to go...

115
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:53,600
You...

116
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:55,840
What time will you be back?

117
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:56,670
I don't know.

118
00:10:13,150 --> 00:10:14,880
You're keeping regular hours.

119
00:10:21,750 --> 00:10:23,880
They clearly have something going on.

120
00:10:37,190 --> 00:10:39,520
You're right.
I don't need to put on an act.

121
00:10:54,190 --> 00:10:55,420
Where should I go?

122
00:10:57,840 --> 00:10:58,900
To the art gallery.

123
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:00,190
Right.

124
00:11:01,150 --> 00:11:02,270
I didn't get a chance to

125
00:11:02,270 --> 00:11:04,900
really look at
Autumn Moon in the Forest last time.

126
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:06,480
Wait.

127
00:11:06,510 --> 00:11:09,070
It's Monday. The museum is closed.

128
00:11:24,290 --> 00:11:25,390
[Hexin Psychological Clinic]

129
00:11:24,740 --> 00:11:26,690
So you two slept together?

130
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,790
Of course not.

131
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:39,120
And besides,

132
00:11:40,390 --> 00:11:42,270
I was talking about my friend.

133
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:46,640
Your friend.

134
00:11:47,870 --> 00:11:48,960
So,

135
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:53,100
your friend kissed her ex-husband,

136
00:11:53,510 --> 00:11:55,080
and that one kiss

137
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:56,640
kept her up all night?

138
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:02,560
And they still live under the same roof.

139
00:12:02,790 --> 00:12:04,670
Now things are awkward,

140
00:12:04,670 --> 00:12:07,000
and she doesn't know
how to act around him?

141
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:07,790
Exactly.

142
00:12:11,690 --> 00:12:12,450
Dr. Xie,

143
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:14,840
where's your professional ethics?

144
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:16,720
Right now,

145
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:18,200
it's my lunch break.

146
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,510
I'm talking to you

147
00:12:20,510 --> 00:12:22,750
as Xie He.

148
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:24,150
I didn't charge you.

149
00:12:25,030 --> 00:12:25,720
Besides,

150
00:12:26,270 --> 00:12:28,320
after living with
her ex-husband for so many years,

151
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,350
she kisses him once

152
00:12:29,350 --> 00:12:32,150
and loses her head so badly
she has to see a therapist?

153
00:12:32,150 --> 00:12:33,600
That's adorable.

154
00:12:34,660 --> 00:12:36,230
It's not like that.

155
00:12:38,390 --> 00:12:40,720
They are not in that kind of relationship.

156
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:42,200
And they're living together now

157
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:42,670
because

158
00:12:42,670 --> 00:12:43,150
there's...

159
00:12:43,150 --> 00:12:45,720
There's a reason they have no choice.

160
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:47,200
Then why don't you get back together?

161
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:49,210
We could never be together again.

162
00:12:57,780 --> 00:13:00,300
I mean my friend.

163
00:13:00,690 --> 00:13:03,380
They stopped loving
each other a long time ago.

164
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,390
My friend especially,

165
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:07,480
and her ex-husband even more.

166
00:13:11,030 --> 00:13:12,930
They don't love each other anymore.

167
00:13:12,930 --> 00:13:14,450
How could they not?

168
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:18,320
Dr. Xie?

169
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:22,510
I mean,

170
00:13:24,050 --> 00:13:25,170
people are

171
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:26,680
creatures of desire.

172
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:28,790
Especially adults.

173
00:13:29,510 --> 00:13:31,840
Desire can be a form of love, too.

174
00:13:32,630 --> 00:13:35,120
But desire can also be about winning.

175
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,790
What if her ex-husband is
just driven by the need to win?

176
00:13:37,790 --> 00:13:38,720
Think about it.

177
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:40,920
Your friend kissed him

178
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:42,480
and still felt completely flustered.

179
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:44,810
That means she still has feelings for him.

180
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,630
Even if she won't admit it,

181
00:13:46,910 --> 00:13:49,000
she can't fake feelings or desire.

182
00:13:50,390 --> 00:13:51,850
You need to get your friend

183
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
to face her most primal desires.

184
00:13:58,930 --> 00:14:00,140
Song Yiqiu,

185
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:03,090
you're avoiding me.

186
00:14:04,630 --> 00:14:07,290
You two have a history
that goes back lifetimes.

187
00:14:08,390 --> 00:14:11,790
Even Lin Huai's reincarnation
couldn't make him forget you.

188
00:14:13,380 --> 00:14:16,260
You wouldn't happen
to be going after him, would you?

189
00:14:16,260 --> 00:14:16,730
Uncle.

190
00:14:20,090 --> 00:14:22,420
Here's all the information on your rival.

191
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:34,740
How do I compare to him?

192
00:14:35,030 --> 00:14:36,560
Am I really that far behind?

193
00:14:39,650 --> 00:14:43,250
He's young, handsome,
highly educated, and a rich heir.

194
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:45,150
His family situation is uncomplicated.

195
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:47,550
He sounds like the perfect boyfriend.

196
00:14:47,550 --> 00:14:48,720
Aren't I?

197
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,640
Maybe for an ordinary person.

198
00:14:55,050 --> 00:14:56,170
But for Ms. Song,

199
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:59,270
you're just an ex-husband
who refuses to disappear.

200
00:14:59,270 --> 00:15:01,240
The secret to love is novelty.

201
00:15:01,510 --> 00:15:03,510
People always go for the new ones...

202
00:15:07,670 --> 00:15:08,840
But,

203
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:10,720
Lin Huai has one fatal flaw,

204
00:15:10,870 --> 00:15:12,670
and it's your only advantage.

205
00:15:15,270 --> 00:15:15,840
Go on.

206
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:19,860
Lin Huai is just an ordinary man.

207
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:21,370
If Ms. Song really falls in love with him,

208
00:15:21,370 --> 00:15:23,360
she'll have, at most,
a few decades with him.

209
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:24,670
And after he dies,

210
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,460
you'll be the only one
left by her side again.

211
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:29,840
Exactly.

212
00:15:31,150 --> 00:15:32,150
That makes sense.

213
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:35,550
But

214
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:37,080
we ordinary people

215
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:39,550
know that life has an end,

216
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:42,000
so we love without holding anything back.

217
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,060
To grow old together and die together

218
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:45,640
with the person you love,

219
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:48,170
that's the most romantic thing

220
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,000
I can imagine.

221
00:16:02,250 --> 00:16:03,710
You need to get your friend

222
00:16:03,950 --> 00:16:05,920
to face her most primal desires.

223
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:15,130
[Ning Changyue]

224
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,800
Isn't it just about human desire?

225
00:16:21,310 --> 00:16:23,040
Who could that possibly scare?

226
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:32,080
She can't fake feelings or desire.

227
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:32,710
♪ Whispers and judging eyes
swirl around us ♪

228
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,460
You need to get your friend

229
00:16:34,570 --> 00:16:36,730
to face her most primal desires.

230
00:16:34,650 --> 00:16:38,210
♪ The dying embers
consume the flames completely ♪

231
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,790
The most primal desires?

232
00:16:47,270 --> 00:16:48,720
I've lived for 3,000 years.

233
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:49,850
What haven't I seen?

234
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:51,680
The most primal desires

235
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:55,080
call for the most primal solution.

236
00:16:56,070 --> 00:16:56,790
Hello.

237
00:16:56,820 --> 00:16:57,950
How many do you want?

238
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:03,550
-Miss.
-Miss.

239
00:17:03,570 --> 00:17:04,640
-Hello, miss!
-Hello, miss!

240
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:05,770
Good evening, Miss.

241
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:07,109
Miss!

242
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:08,270
Come on, Miss.

243
00:17:09,750 --> 00:17:10,400
Come on, bottoms up.

244
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:11,720
Have a drink.

245
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:12,490
Drink up.

246
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:13,910
A toast to you, Miss.

247
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,240
Come on, Miss.

248
00:17:18,390 --> 00:17:19,960
Have some watermelon.

249
00:17:20,950 --> 00:17:22,560
Here, have another piece.

250
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:04,480
Yu Tu,

251
00:18:05,070 --> 00:18:06,030
is Qiu back yet?

252
00:18:07,830 --> 00:18:08,790
No.

253
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:10,740
It's so late, and it's raining.

254
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:12,340
Where on earth did she go?

255
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:13,200
Where's Madam?

256
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:14,460
Tell her to come see me.

257
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:15,650
M-Master.

258
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:16,180
Madam, she...

259
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:17,640
You're worried about her?

260
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,590
Then go find her.

261
00:18:19,890 --> 00:18:20,750
What happened to her?

262
00:18:20,750 --> 00:18:21,270
Speak.

263
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:22,550
Madam, she...

264
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:23,720
ran away.

265
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:25,440
Then bring her back.

266
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:28,360
Madam said she never
wants to see you again.

267
00:18:28,750 --> 00:18:29,980
She's 3,000 years old.

268
00:18:29,980 --> 00:18:30,960
She's not even afraid of death.

269
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:32,490
Why would I worry about her?

270
00:18:40,640 --> 00:18:42,080
I'm going out for a walk.

271
00:18:44,670 --> 00:18:47,060
Stubborn to the very end.

272
00:19:08,510 --> 00:19:10,790
Why is it raining in the bathroom?

273
00:19:32,310 --> 00:19:34,940
♪ Watch me die ♪

274
00:19:35,260 --> 00:19:36,950
♪ Fall and rise ♪

275
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:39,950
♪ I am brave ♪

276
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:44,700
♪ You will find, find your way ♪

277
00:19:45,570 --> 00:19:48,190
♪ No matter if you win or lose ♪
